    <string name="about_acknowledgements">Acknowledgements</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_title">Special thanks</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_subtitle">The projects and people behind Polylute</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_pixelplayer">To PixelPlayer, for a beautiful app worth falling in love with.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_decent_player">To decent-player, for the USB driver that lets the music reach the DAC untouched.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_playback">To Media3, FFmpeg (via Jellyfin) and libFLAC, for playing every file we throw at them.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_tags">To TagLib and JAudiotagger, for reading our libraries right.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_fiio">To WolfEQ and Pragmatic Audio\'s DevicePEQ, for mapping the FiiO EQ protocol.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_music_data">To LRCLIB and MusicBrainz, for keeping music data open.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_interface">To Wavy Slider, Reorderable and Coil, for the little things that feel right.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_licenses">And to every project in Licenses: Polylute stands on your work.</string>
    <string name="about_special_thanks_roderick">And to Roderick, who got me into the audio world, helped me understand every concept along the way, and was brave enough to try it, beer in hand, long before it was anywhere near finished.</string>
